      "message": "That is absolutely right and is a nasty bug. As discussed offline, the nice thing is that this series handles np-guest permission faults from user_mem_abort(), which marks the page dirty during write faults, so we do not in fact need make the page dirty here as well. And luckily, if we leave the dirty state untouched here, we can simply call unpin_user_pages() which doesn\u0027t block. I\u0027ll update.",
